Clearview - Weather through the eyes of the world

Clearview is a modern web application that reimagines the weather forecast. Instead of just looking at numbers, users can see what the weather actually looks like through real-time "Weather Moments" shared by a global community.

Features

Real-Time Visuals: View "Trending Weather Moments" from cities like San Diego, Seattle, and Aspen.
Hyper-Local Data: Detailed current conditions for your specific location, including:
Wind Speed, Humidity, and Visibility.
"Feels Like" temperature and Atmospheric Ambience audio.
7-Day Forecast: A clean, scannable outlook for the week ahead.
Personalized Dashboard: Save and track weather for your favorite cities (e.g., Los Angeles, New York, Miami).
Community Sharing: A dedicated portal for users to upload their own weather photos and videos.

Technology Stack

Frontend: Built with modern HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.
Icons & Assets: FontAwesome integration for weather-specific iconography.
Audio: Integrated background ambience (e.g., Clear Sky Ambience) for an immersive experience.

Project Structure

Home: Main dashboard featuring local weather and the 7-day forecast.
Explore: Discover weather moments from around the globe.
Locations: Manage your saved cities and personalized alerts.
Community: Connect with other "weather watchers" and view top-rated moments.

Getting Started

Search: Use the global search bar to find any location worldwide.
Save: Click the heart icon on any city to add it to your "Saved Locations."
Share: Use the "Share Moment" button to contribute to the global weather feed.



Technical Setup

Follow these steps to get a local development instance of Clearview up and running on your machine.

1. Prerequisites

Ensure you have a modern web browser and a local server environment (like Python's http.server, Live Server for VS Code, or Node.js) installed.

2. Clone the Repository
Bash

git clone https://github.com/yourusername/clearview.git
cd clearview

3. Launch the Application

Depending on your preferred environment, run one of the following commands in your terminal:
Using Python (Quickest):Bashpython -m http.server 8000

Using Node.js (serve):Bashnpx serve .

4. Access the Site

Once the server is running, open your browser and navigate to:
http://127.0.0.1:8000/

